      "writtenOn": "2021-06-22T22:02:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Brian, I am not sure what I should to to address this comment. This is in a different branch (cr50_stab vs main) and for a different chip (h1 vs stm32). \n\nNote that there also is a Rust implementaion in the Ti50 project ;).\n\nIt is possible to unify protocol implementation and move it to ./common, but I am not sure if stm32 SPI controller  would provide the necessary API, and even then there would be two implementaions in two different branches.\n\n\u003e There\u0027s going to be a non-insignificant number of changes from the need to remove the memory buffer. \n\nI am not sure I follow: this patch does not require any additional memory buffers, which is an advantage for Cr50 which is pretty strained for both ROM and RAM.",
      "parentUuid": "d3425762_fa8bfe27",
      "revId": "ba52101e5dada84479edcdc949a9a823653533b7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
